    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d612">

                <pb facs="0676" n="418" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg418"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 300.115N27/8</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">
                        The Consul at Liverpool</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Washington</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Liverpool</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-05-28T08:00:00+00:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">May 28, 1915, 8 a. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 8.15 a. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Nebraskan</hi> chartered White Star Line, water ballast.
                    Shock followed by explosion 8.24 evening May 25, latitude 51.14 N., longitude
                    10.52 W. Captain and officer watch say flag lowered ten minutes before
                    explosion. Chief engineer only person saw track approaching torpedo. Captain,
                    officer watch, and chief engineer say light time explosion sufficient see two
                    thousand feet. Name and port painted both sides letters six feet high.
                    Lieutenant Towers, Constructor McBride making further examination <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Nebraskan</hi> to-day. They will photograph in dry dock
                    next week.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
